<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - see Disposition__c.field-meta.xml
        in this folder for why a comment above the root breaks `sf` deploy.

        2026-08-21 - VALUE SET CONFIRMED BY THE USER (was design D4.2 / O-2, flagged OPEN in
        every prior deploy of this file - now closed). Six values, "Initial Appointment" added
        FIRST: Initial Appointment, Performance Issue, Better BOV Received, Broker Withdrew,
        Company Decision, Other. This is the FINAL value set; do not re-flag it as open.

        WHY "Initial Appointment" WAS ADDED (design doc agent-output/bov-scoring-and-selection.md
        §4.2): every one of the five original values presupposes a predecessor broker being
        replaced. BovSubmissionService.replaceSelectedBroker already degrades cleanly to an
        "appoint" when there is no current incumbent and still writes a history row
        unconditionally - so a first appointment was always going to produce a row here, and
        without this value it could only be logged as "Other", the un-attributed row this whole
        workstream exists to prevent.

        WHY NOT Broker_Assignment__c.Reason_Ended__c's VALUE SET, DELIBERATELY: that field is
        {Leased Up, Performance Issue, Company Decision, Other}. "Leased Up" is leasing
        vocabulary (a listing ending because the space leased) and is meaningless on a
        disposition BOV, which is a sale-side broker swap. Copying it verbatim would ship a
        picklist value that can never correctly apply to any row on this object.

        restricted=true, matching Submission_Status__c on BOV_Submission__c and this repo's
        general practice for closed-set reason/status fields - it stops a hand-typed value the
        six confirmed options do not cover, which is also why "Other" still exists as the escape
        hatch. ⚠ Restricted picklists ARE enforced by Apex DML in this org (measured twice on
        this project) - an off-list value throws INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST, so
        "Initial Appointment" must exist in metadata and be deployed BEFORE any code sends it.
        Adding a value is safe under a restricted picklist; removing or relabelling one would
        fail at DML rather than at an assertion - not attempted here, only an addition.
    -->
    <fullName>Reason__c</fullName>
    <description>Why the broker was replaced or first appointed. Six confirmed values; see the XML comment in this file for why "Initial Appointment" was added.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pick the closest reason. Use Other if none fit, and add detail in Notes.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Reason</label>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Picklist</type>
    <valueSet>
        <restricted>true</restricted>
        <valueSetDefinition>
            <sorted>false</sorted>
            <value>
                <fullName>Initial Appointment</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Initial Appointment</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Performance Issue</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Performance Issue</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Better BOV Received</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Better BOV Received</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Broker Withdrew</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Broker Withdrew</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Company Decision</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Company Decision</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>Other</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>Other</label>
            </value>
        </valueSetDefinition>
    </valueSet>
</CustomField>
